    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0367" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1462</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 16, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.35 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Swedish Government last night sent notes of protest to England and Germany
                    regarding condition of neutral shipping at sea. Norwegian Minister
                    confidentially informs me this morning that Norwegian and Danish Governments
                    will file identical notes to-day and that these notes similar to American
                    notes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
